        "description": "Newsbeat's Pete Allison explains what would happen if Australia won the Eurovision Song Contest, as the country returns in 2026 with one of its biggest stars, Delta Goodrem.\n\nDespite competing in Eurovision for more than a decade, Australia can't host the contest if it wins. Instead, organisers say a European country would be chosen to stage the following year\u2019s event on Australia\u2019s behalf - most likely one of the contest\u2019s biggest financial contributors, such as France or Germany.\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\n#Eurovision #Australia #BBCNews #DeltaGoodrem #Eurovision2026 #BBCNews",
